==Strategy==
Getting rid of the Le'boin fast is crucial to succeeding in this stage, as the Gabriels get strong fast, and they can quickly overwhelm you, even if the Le'boin is already dead.

The best way to approach this stage is to take as little time as possible killing the Le'Boin, which means using backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] or any ubers that are able to deal good damage to Le'Boin. To deal with the Gabriels, constantly spamming [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] is a good idea, since they spawn so frequently and are just fragile enough to the point that money will not be an issue in this stage.

On higher crown difficulties, a ''very'' well-timed [[Talents|Talented]] Awakened Bahamut Cat is all you need to take out Le'boin in record time. Finding an opening may prove difficult, however, due to unpredictability caused by the Gabriels and their many knockbacks.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Axis of Evil]] stages, Celestial Seas has a Russian-themed Japanese name. In this case, Batoru Umi no Kessen (バトル海の決戦, "Showdown on the Battle Sea"), is a pun on Baruto Umi no Tatakai (バルト海の戦い, "Battle on the Baltic Sea"), the Japanese name for a series of fights between the Russian and German armies that occurred on the Baltic Sea during World War I.

